### --------------------------------------------------------
### Import Endpoints (Operator — Tier 2)
### Requires: X-Security, X-App-Name (admin), X-Operator-Key
### --------------------------------------------------------

### Import tokens — JSON body
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-001",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "expiresAt": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
  },
  {
    "userId": "user-002",
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]

### Import tokens — CSV body
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: text/csv
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

userId,appName,expiresAt
user-003,myapp,2027-12-31T23:59:59Z
user-004,myapp,

### Import tokens — per-app (JSON, no appName in items)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/myapp
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-005",
    "expiresAt": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
  },
  {
    "userId": "user-006"
  }
]

### Import tokens — per-app (CSV, no appName column)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/myapp
Content-Type: text/csv
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

userId,expiresAt
user-007,2027-12-31T23:59:59Z
user-008,

### Import tokens — without userId (auto-generated UUID)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "appName": "myapp",
    "expiresAt": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
  },
  {
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]

### Import tokens — per-app without userId (auto-generated UUID)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/myapp
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {},
  {
    "expiresAt": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
  }
]

### Import tokens — CSV without userId (auto-generated UUID)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: text/csv
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

appName,expiresAt
myapp,2027-12-31T23:59:59Z
myapp,

### Re-issue without userId → should fail (400) — userId is required for reissue
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/reissue
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]

### Import — duplicate userId+appName with active token (should return in errors[])
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-001",
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]

### Import — re-import after revocation (revoked token should be replaced)
# First revoke user-001's token via POST /tokens/:id/revoke, then run this
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-001",
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]

### --------------------------------------------------------
### Custom Token Import (Operator — Tier 2)
### Operator provides their own token strings.
### A custom token is any string 4–64 chars — no app-name prefix required.
### The token is verified against the app it was imported under (header), not its text.
### --------------------------------------------------------

### Import with custom token — JSON body
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-custom-001",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "token": "CustomSecretToken001"
  }
]

### Import with custom token — CSV body
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: text/csv
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

userId,appName,token
user-custom-002,myapp,AnotherCustomTok02

### Import with custom token — per-app (appName from URL)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/myapp
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-custom-003",
    "token": "PerAppCustomTok003"
  }
]

### Import with custom token — invalid format (too short < 4 chars, should be in errors[])
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-custom-bad",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "token": "ab"
  }
]

### Import with custom token — too long (> 64 chars, should be in errors[])
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-custom-bad2",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "token": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
  }
]

### Import with custom token — duplicate (run after first custom import; should be in errors[])
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-custom-dup",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "token": "CustomSecretToken001"
  }
]

### Re-issue with custom token (replaces active token with operator-provided one)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/reissue
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-custom-001",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "token": "ReissuedCustomTk01"
  }
]

### --------------------------------------------------------
### Re-Issue Endpoint (Operator — Tier 2)
### Replaces existing tokens (active or revoked) with new ones
### --------------------------------------------------------

### Re-issue tokens — JSON body
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/reissue
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-001",
    "appName": "myapp",
    "expiresAt": "2027-12-31T23:59:59Z"
  },
  {
    "userId": "user-002",
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]

### Re-issue tokens — CSV body
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/reissue
Content-Type: text/csv
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

userId,appName,expiresAt
user-001,myapp,2027-12-31T23:59:59Z
user-002,myapp,

### Re-issue — user with no existing token (should work like normal import)
POST {{$dotenv HOST}}/import/reissue
Content-Type: application/json
X-Security: {{$dotenv SECURITY_KEY}}
X-App-Name: {{$dotenv ADMIN_APP_NAME}}
X-Operator-Key: {{$dotenv OPERATOR_KEY}}

[
  {
    "userId": "user-new-reissue",
    "appName": "myapp"
  }
]
